I am doing my first project on SEM. I am pretty clear on all the underlying concepts and mathematical equations for the technique. However, what I require is to run the model in R and use the estimates to make prediction in excel by forming a mathematical equation incorporating all the coefficients. To clarify my point further, I will take the example used in lavaan package pdf. So, I have the following model:

model <- '
# measurement model
ind60 =~ x1 + x2 + x3
dem60 =~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4
dem65 =~ y5 + y6 + y7 + y8
# regressions
dem60 ~ ind60
dem65 ~ ind60 + dem60
# residual correlations
y1 ~~ y5
y2 ~~ y4 + y6
y3 ~~ y7
y4 ~~ y8
y6 ~~ y8
'

After running a SEM model on it, I get the following estimates:

