Okay...I've got a question on using mat.regress for getting the regression equations. We know that SEM uses a set of equations (measurement model and structural model) to predict Y. For instance, below are the theoretical equations used in the model:

# measurement model
ind60 =~ x1 + x2 + x3.....(1)
dem60 =~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4.....(2)
dem65 =~ y5 + y6 + y7 + y8....(3)
# structural model
dem60 ~ ind60.....(4)
dem65 ~ ind60 + dem60....(5)

To get the regression scores for each equation, I will be entering the covariance matrix for each of them and getting the beta coefficients.Is this the right way to go?

