Regarding your 3rd question, lavPredict is for calculating factor scores.  Read the "Details" section of the ?lavPredict help page to see "that this function can not be used to ‘predict’ values of dependent variables, given the values of independent values (in the regression sense)."  Although you could manually calculate predicted probabilities of the outcome given your model parameters and any specified levels of your predictors (including the factor scores provided by lavPredict), bear in mind that the latent variables are not observed.  So the predicted probabilities have additional uncertainty due to factor indeterminacy.  You might want to post this topic on SEMNET  <http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html>to get advice about assessing the predictive quality of a latent-variable model.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
UvA web page: http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

